I'm trying to build NetHack 4 locally so I can hack on the source a
bit, but aimake seems to be misbehaving somehow. This is on Arch Linux.

jansson and zlib are both installed, but when I run aimake, I get a
message insinuating that they are lacking (sorry for butchering lines):

| The following rules did not run due to missing dependencies:
|
| compile_c on object path:nethack_server/src/db_pgsql.c:
file:libpq-fe.h(nethack_server/src/db_pgsql.c)
| link_c on object bpath:nethack_server/src/srvmain.o:
check_database(nethack_server/src/srvmain.o),
close_database(nethack_server/src/srvmain.o),
compress(libnethack/src/log.o), and 42 more objects
| link_c on object bpath:nethack/src/main.o:
compress(libnethack/src/log.o), compressBound(libnethack/src/log.o),
json_array(libnethack_client/src/clientapi.o), and 23 more objects

The full output can be found at http://pastebin.com/nYi8htbP

I imagine the first two messages are just because I didn't install
postgresql (not intending to build the server just yet). The refusal
to link main is puzzling, though, because I can link it just fine by
hand, if I use the appropriate flags:

  $ gcc -o nethack4 nethack/src/*.o libnethack/src/*.o \
    libnethack_client/src/*.o libuncursed/src/tty.o \
    libuncursed/src/uncursed.o -lm -lz -ljansson

and before I know it I'm dying to a water moccasin on dlvl 1 just like
old times.

Why does it think that those dependencies are missing? I've poked
through the source (of aimake) and I guess it probably has to do with
my (i.e., Arch's) version of gcc or ld having a slightly different
output format, but I don't know what format aimake expects nor how to
fix it. What commands could I run to help narrow down this problem?

